  <div class="section no-top-padding"><div class="container"><div class="hero4 hero-content-centered"><div class="subtitle">January 21, 2023</div><h1>Things to do around Toile Blanche</h1></div></div></div><div class="full-frame-image-wrapper" style='background-image:url("https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/639af6c370637a84eae3b0bb/63de6a1d6f6edd144558999e_anthony-salerno-f_gJ1Hof7rs-unsplash-min.jpg")'></div><div class="section"><div class="container"><div class="blog-post w-richtext"><p>Hotel Toile Blanche is located in the charming town of Vence, in the French Riviera. The area surrounding the hotel offers a variety of activities and attractions for visitors to enjoy.</p><p>For those interested in art, the Fondation Maeght is a must-see. This modern art museum features works by famous artists such as Joan Miro and Marc Chagall. The Matisse Chapel, located nearby, is another popular destination for art lovers, featuring a series of colorful mosaics created by Henri Matisse.</p><p>‍</p><figure class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image" style="max-width:5616pxpx"><div><img alt="" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-0bd0acfefc8c5b.jpg"/></div></figure><p>‍</p><p>Outdoor enthusiasts will appreciate the many hiking and biking trails in the surrounding hills. The Sentier des Douaniers, a coastal hiking trail, offers breathtaking views of the Mediterranean Sea. For a more strenuous hike, the Chemin de Saint-Jacques de Compostelle is a popular trail that leads to the summit of Mont Gros.</p><p>Vence is also known for its delicious local cuisine. The hotel's restaurant, Le Toile Blanche, serves a variety of traditional Provencal dishes made with fresh, locally sourced ingredients. Other nearby restaurants worth visiting include La Table de Suzanne and La Mere Germaine.</p><p>‍</p><figure class="w-richtext-align-fullwidth w-richtext-figure-type-image" style="max-width:3275px"><div><img alt="" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-92dbcf00dca22c.jpg"/></div></figure><p>‍</p><p>The charming town center of Vence is also worth a visit. The Place du Grand Jardin is a lovely spot to relax and take in the sights and sounds of the town. The Saint-Paul de Vence, a fortified medieval village, is also nearby and definitely worth a visit.</p><p>Overall, Hotel Toile Blanche offers an ideal base for exploring the charming town of Vence and the surrounding French Riviera. With its proximity to art museums, outdoor activities, and delicious local cuisine, there is something for everyone in the area.</p><p>‍</p><p>‍</p></div></div></div><div class="section no-top-padding"><div class="container"><div class="heading-wrapper inner-spacing div-block"><h2>Continue reading</h2></div></div><div class="container no-padding-mobile"><div class="blog-collection-list-wrapper w-dyn-list"><div class="blog-flex-thirds w-dyn-items" role="list"><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="self-guided-tour-itinarary.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="A self-guided tour itinerary of the area surrounding Hotel Toile Blanche in Vence, French Riviera." class="image-cover" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" src="/assets/images/page-img-4096fb7a8a053f.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">A self-guided tour itinerary of the area surrounding Hotel Toile Blanche in Vence, French Riviera.</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="10-best-swimmig-holes.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="10 Best Swimming Holes at (and around) Toile Blanche" class="image-cover" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" src="/assets/images/page-img-0bd0acfefc8c5b.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">10 Best Swimming Holes at (and around) Toile Blanche</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div><div class="blog-item w-dyn-item" role="listitem"><a class="collection-link-block w-inline-block" href="wine-lovers.html"><div class="collection-image-wrapper"><img alt="Wine lovers, rejoice! The French Riviera is home to some of the world's most renowned vineyards" class="image-cover" loading="lazy" sizes="100vw" src="/assets/images/page-img-0bd0acfefc8c5b.jpg"/></div><div class="collection-content-wrapper"><div class="subtitle">Wine lovers, rejoice! The French Riviera is home to some of the world's most renowned vineyards</div><img alt="" class="collection-arrow-img" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/page-img-a926ac09f8f7bc.svg"/></div></a></div></div></div></div></div>

